From: RetroArch-PI
Subject: [PATCH] main: cached interpreter for GoldenEye 007 and Perfect Dark

Both crash the ARM64 new_dynarec: RetroArch exits with SIGTRAP (status 133)
within 2 s of "Init new dynarec", with any GFX plugin and with or without
the Expansion Pak. Other big N64 games (Conker, Banjo-Tooie, Majora's Mask)
run fine on the dynarec. The cached interpreter runs GoldenEye's intro at
96-100% on a KickPi K2B (H618 @ 1512 MHz). Select it automatically for
these two cartridge IDs ("GE", "PD"), logging a warning.

---
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/main/main.c
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/main/main.c
@@ -320,6 +320,25 @@
    /* take the r4300 emulator mode from the config file at this point and cache it in a global variable */
    unsigned int emumode = ConfigGetParamInt(g_CoreConfig, "R4300Emulator");
 
+   /* RetroArch-PI: GoldenEye 007 and Perfect Dark crash the ARM64 new_dynarec
+    * (SIGTRAP within 2 s of "Init new dynarec", with any GFX plugin and with
+    * or without the Expansion Pak; both run their game code from TLB-mapped
+    * memory). Run them on the cached interpreter instead: GoldenEye's intro
+    * measured 96-100% on an H618 (4x A53 @ 1.5 GHz). Matched on the
+    * cartridge ID (header bytes 0x3C-0x3D, "GE" / "PD"), which every region
+    * of each game shares, so it works whatever the ROM file is called. */
+   if (emumode >= 2)
+   {
+      const unsigned char *cid = (const unsigned char *)&ROM_HEADER.Cartridge_ID;
+      if ((cid[0] == 'G' && cid[1] == 'E') || (cid[0] == 'P' && cid[1] == 'D'))
+      {
+         DebugMessage(M64MSG_WARNING,
+               "%s (ID %c%c): the dynamic recompiler crashes on this game, using the cached interpreter",
+               ROM_PARAMS.headername, cid[0], cid[1]);
+         emumode = 1;
+      }
+   }
+
    /* set some other core parameters based on the config file values */
    no_compiled_jump = ConfigGetParamBool(g_CoreConfig, "NoCompiledJump");
    disable_extra_mem = ConfigGetParamInt(g_CoreConfig, "DisableExtraMem");
